      "message": "Are we guaranteed uid is always \u003c 10043 ? Maybe it can\u0027t ever be \u003c 10000, but I expect it might be 10042 at least in principle, or if not then it depends on how many apps are installed on the device.\n\nA simple way to not have to care would be to say something like\n\n  private UidRange[] uidRangesFor(int... uids) {\n    Arrays.sort(uids);\n    final UidRange[] ranges \u003d new UidRange[uids.length - 1]; // crash if length \u003d\u003d 0\n    for (int i \u003d 0; i \u003c ranges.length; ++i) {\n      ranges[i] \u003d new UidRange(uids[i], uids[i + 1]);\n    }\n    return ranges;\n  }\n\n...then you get a UidRange[] that you can pass to the vararg expected by expectNRJNSV",
